<h1>vroxy Rails demo</h1>

<p>
  Signed in as
  <strong><%= current_user ? "#{current_user.name} (#{current_user.role})" : "nobody" %></strong>.
</p>

<ul>
  <li><a href="/?as=member">as a member</a></li>
  <li><a href="/?as=admin">as an admin</a> — also loads the UI-feedback inspector</li>
  <li><a href="/?as=anonymous">anonymous</a> — loader only, no identify call</li>
  <li><a href="/billing">/billing</a> — another page, same auto-injected snippet</li>
  <li><a href="/up">/up</a> — on <code>exclude_paths</code>, never injected</li>
</ul>

<h2>Rendered partials</h2>
<ul>
  <%= render partial: "tip", collection: ["signed identify unlocks admin-only bot tools",
                                          "this list is rendered from a partial"], as: :tip %>
</ul>

<p>
  View source: the tags before <code>&lt;/body&gt;</code> are what the gem added.
  As an admin, the inspector's <code>rendered_partials</code> lists the partial above.
</p>
